<https://w3id.org/aias> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Alexander Fay" .
<https://w3id.org/aias#EdgeDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Edge-Gerät"@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias#hasCommunication> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A communication describes the exchange of information between at least two resources, and an instance of it is tied to the components taking part, which makes the technical realisation of a data flow explicit.\r\n\r\nThe two relations below differentiate the direction. They are not subproperties of this one: a sensor that only sends carries hasOutputCommunication and nothing else, and a reasoner that inferred hasCommunication from it would report the sensor as bidirectional, which is the opposite of what the model states.\r\n\r\nThe domain is the component rather than the resource on purpose. A product may take part in a communication as well: a workpiece carrying an RFID tag or a barcode is read along the line, and restricting the relation to resources would rule that out."@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Physical objects created, changed or consumed in the course of a technical process."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Nothing here is normative. The three patterns rest on standards, this ontology rests on design decisions of the work.\r\n\r\nThree subdomains are joined: the technical process after VDI 3682, the communication after ISO/IEC 7498-1, and the AI after ISO/IEC 22989.\r\n\r\nScope: the three patterns named above and the classes that tie them together. The payload of a transmission is equated with a dataset rather than kept apart from it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias#Controller> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias#Actuator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias#Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/aias#hasOutputCommunication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Describes a unidirectional use as a sender."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias#hasRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AISystem> .
